do you know what the realm is it's the  thousand blades of aegon's enemies  a story we agree to tell each other over  and over till we forget that it's a lie  what's up ladies and gentlemen welcome  back for another song of ice and fire  video  in this video i want to mostly talk  about what happened on the night aegon  the conqueror brought fire and blood to  the enormous castle known as harrenhal  as you all know the upcoming hbo series  house of the dragon will  be based on george r martin's book fire  and blood  in my last video i said i wanted to  start making videos on the chapters from  fire and blood because there is a good  chance we could learn more about this  information  in the new series house of the dragon as  i was reading the first chapter in fire  and blood i decided i would make this  video based on some of the information  given  in that first chapter which covers  aegon's conquest  this is one of the many scenes i would  love to see brought to life on the  television screen  now even if you haven't read any of the  books i am sure most of you will  remember harrenhal from game of thrones  all of you should remember the location  because this is where jaime revealed  what happened during the night he  executed the mad king  this is where brienne fought the bear  and this is also where arya shared many  scenes with tywin lannister  and jack nagar i think this is one of  the most fascinating castles in all of  the seven kingdoms  however if you have only seen game of  thrones then you might not know that  much about why this castle now looks  like a graveyard  the show did give us a basic description  about what happened here  but in this video i want to go over some  of the more interesting details about  the castle  in that historical event  greatest fortress ever built tallest  towers the strongest walls  the great hall had 35 paths  35 can you imagine the man who is  responsible for commanding the  construction of the largest castle in  westeros  which set right on the northern shore of  the god's eye was known as harren horror  also known as heron the black he was the  last of the kings of the isles  and the rivers to rule over the iron  islands and the riverlands  one thing i want to do is give you a  sense of just how massive harrenhal was  because it's just absolutely insane  it's said that harrenhal is the biggest  castle in westeros  but what exactly does that mean well  it's also said that harrenhal's chambers  were built on a scale that would be more  suitable for giants than your average  man  harrenhal actually has the largest  chamber in westeros  larger than the iron throne room and the  red key the castle has these five  massive towers that makes it look as if  the castle has  fingers reaching for the sky harren hall  actually covers three times the amount  of land winterfell does  and where winterfell only has three  acres for its godswood  harrenhal has 20 acres of land for its  godswood  now one of the details that really  struck a nerve with me is how heron the  black ordered men to cut down  three thousand-year-old werewood so he  can use them as rafters  and beams in his castle this castle  actually has  kitchens that are roughly the same size  as winterfell's great hall  and it also has stables that can house a  thousand horses  many also believe that this castle could  garrison  1 million men basically everything about  this castle  is off the charts by the time harrenhal  was finished  heron the black was an old man who now  had gray hair  because the construction of this castle  lasted for nearly  40 years now although herron's house had  full control over these lands for three  generations  the men of this region had no love for  their ironborn leaders  heron the black had sent thousands of  men to an early grave  during the construction of his great  castle harrenhal  you see king heron had enslaved the  riverlands to raise the mightiest  fortress westeros had ever seen  now in order to build something that big  there has to be a lot  and i mean a lot of resources this  is one of the many reasons why he  started to lose support by the time  aegon's conquest began  when you consider the amount of lives  that were lost and the amount of  resources in that area that were used up  during the construction of heron hall  you can start to see why the riverlands  he once ruled over  were now beginning to rise up against  him now what's really interesting is  on the same exact day the new castle was  finally finished  aegon targaryen landed at the mouth of  the blackwater rush  to start his conquest to westeros herron  the black  in his newly built castle was about to  face their greatest test  so as aegon and his sisters were gearing  up for an attack on harrenhal  harren the black summoned lord edmund  tawley of riverrun  but as i said before since the  riverlands were beginning to rise up  against hair in the black  instead of defending harrenhal lord  edmund talley declared for house  targaryen instead  he raised a dragon banner over his  castle then rode  forth with his knights and archers to  join aegon the dragon  that was a big moment for everyone else  in the riverlands because that gave them  another reason to abandon hair and the  black  and join forces with aegon targaryen  that's exactly what happened  the blackwoods the malistars the vances  the freys the brackens and many others  descended on harrenhal  rather than defend it as soon as king  heron the black realized he was  outnumbered  he took refuge in what he thought was  the greatest fortress in all the lands  heron the black laughed as he locked his  gates and settled down with his  remaining sons  and supporters to withstand a siege he  was confident that aegon and his men  were no match for the castle  he did have an unlimited supply of water  massive vaults stalked with food  and giant walls of stone that were  higher than any ladder  and too thick to be broken by any  battering ram or shattered by any  trebuchet  he was ready for this day or so he  thought  you see harrenhal may have been able to  withstand an assault from all the armies  in westeros combined  but this great fortress was no match for  dragon fire  right after heron locked himself in a  castle aegon sent his maester to the  gates under a peace banner so they could  negotiate  hair in the black went out to meet him  looking all old and gray  yet still fierce in his black armor both  of the kings had their maester in  attendance  so the words that they exchanged are  still remembered  yield now aegon began and you may remain  as lord of the iron islands  yield now and your sons will live to  rule after you  i have 8 000 men outside your walls  what is outside my walls is no concern  to me said hair in the black  my walls are strong and thick aegon  responded by saying  but not so high to keep out dragons  dragons fly  i built them in stone said hair in the  black stone does not burn  aegon ends the conversation by saying  when the sun sets  your line shall end it is said that  heron sped at that  and then walked back to his castle as  soon as he was inside  he sent all of his men outside to defend  the castle  he offered lands and gold to any man who  could bring down the dragon  he also said if i had a daughter you  could have her as well  now that edmund tully had joined forces  with aegon  harren the black then said instead i  will give the man who brings down the  dragon  one of the tally's daughters or all  three of them if he likes  it makes no difference to me herron the  black was ready for war  right as the sun was about to set herron  the black's men stared out into the  darkness  holding on to their weapons knowing what  was about to happen next  after another few moments had went by  they thought that maybe aegon had  left maybe his threats were hollow but  aegon targaryen had something else in  mind  on the back of his dragon valeria on the  black dread he went up into the sky  as high as he could up and up and up  until the dragon looked as if it were no  bigger than a fly sitting upon the moon  only then did he descend well inside the  castle walls  belarion the dread was blacker than the  night sky  moving through the air like a missile as  he dove through the clouds  when he had the castle in his sights the  dragon erupted like a volcano  as his fire rained down upon them stone  walls do not burn  hair in the black said but his castle  was not made of stone alone  wood and hemp and straw and bread salted  beef and  grain were all set ablaze hair and the  black's iron men were not made of stone  either  smoking screaming and shrouded in flames  they ran across the yard and fell from  the walls to die upon the ground below  even the stone began to crack and melt  when the fire became hot enough  the riverlords outside the castle wall  said later that the five great towers of  harrenhal glowed red against the night  like five great candles melting up in  the sky  heron the black and his remaining sons  died in the fire that engulfed his  enormous castle that night  his entire house died with him on the  very next day  as they were standing outside the  smoking ruins of harrenhal  king aegon targaryen accepted fealthy  from edmund talley  lord of riverrun and named him the lord  paramount of the trident  when the ashes had cooled enough to  allow the men to enter the castle safely  the swords of the fallen many shattered  or melted steel by dragon fire  were gathered up and sent back to the  aegon fort and wagons  later to become some of the swords that  would make up the iron throne  the realm do you know what the realm is  it's the thousand blades of aegon's  enemies  a story we agreed to tell each other  over  and over till we forget that it's a lie  [Music]  you
 

